$title
$underline

Teserra is a C++20 game engine for 2D games: https://github.com/fyernald/teserra

This package holds the examples of Teserra $version, each in a folder of its own.

Running them
------------
1. Unzip this folder anywhere (for example, your Desktop).
2. Open an example's folder and double-click its .exe.
3. Press Escape or close the window to quit.

Windows may show a "Windows protected your PC" (SmartScreen) message, because the programs are new and not
code-signed. Choose "More info", then "Run anyway". The programs do not install anything and only write
teserra.log into their own folder.

Requirements: 64-bit Windows 10 or 11 and a graphics driver with OpenGL 4.5 (most GPUs since 2014 with
current drivers). The Visual C++ runtime they need is included.

The examples
------------
$examples

Feedback
--------
Please tell us how it went, even if everything worked:
$feedback_url

Useful to include: what you saw, your Windows version, your GPU and driver version, and the teserra.log file
from the example's folder (it lists the GPU and OpenGL version and any error).

